        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-02T16:18:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way in which this signal is used, it is sufficient to have the pin configured either as open drain or push-pull. But, if it\u0027s configured as open drain, then it should be ODR_LOW, instead of GPIO_INPUT_PULL_UP which itself is correct for an active low interrupt signal.\n\nFrom the ANX7452\u0027s perspective these 2 pins (USB_EN/DP_EN) would be in a hi-z state.\n\nTo me, it would be the cleanest to configure both USB_EN and DP_EN as GPIO_OUTPUT (which I believe defaults to a low level) when the ANX7452 DB is present. We don\u0027t need these signals to be open drain for correct operation.",
      "parentUuid": "ea5618ba_5fa13aa6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "b4b5bf9f6bd6a9c8962712a1745895a74e95cb27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "551ff57f_92d39954",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/rex/rex/src/usb_mux_config.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-02T18:00:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The GPIO is not initialised until this line is triggered if there is analogix DB in the SKU. We are overriding the GPIO definition in generated.dtsi file with no-auto-init device tree configuration in rex.dtsi file. So pull up is not involved in the process. Based on the role of DP_EN GPIO, output low seems to be user friendly among all options, as suggested above.",
